B5 patch for the RL dry run 1 job request (ours: saitej123/era-v5-lab#139, head 1bd2df53). NOT applied anywhere yet:
apply once the lead agrees to switch the sampler, and only after the B5 PR (g5_decode.sample_many, sampler kind g5_batch) is
merged into the base, because train.py refuses g5_batch without it.

Why (results/b5_sampler_2026-11-23.md): with sampler policy the job decodes its 16 prompts one after another; on a T4 at the
job's settings r = 44.3 s per prompt's 8 samples, above the 9.4 s the job's time table goes to, so after the SFT rebuild the
enough_time rule would take the screen-only branch. g5_batch is 12.8x faster on the same T4 (r = 3.45 s).

What it changes in capstone/rl_job_v1.py (default stays policy, so nothing changes unless the flag is passed):
  --sampler {policy,g5_batch}, --sampler-max-rows (default 128) -> written into rl_config.yaml (train.sampler,
  train.sampler_max_rows); under g5_batch the rate probe times ONE bundle.sample_many over the rate-probe prompts (real stops,
  bf16 autocast on cuda) instead of the per-prompt screen, and the SFT rebuild's per-prompt rate is not used.
Tested at 1bd2df53 + this patch (+ the B5 rl-loop files overlaid): capstone/test_rl_job_v1.py 17 passed; batched_rate on the
CPU stand-in returned r = 0.171 s (4 prompts, k 2, 32 new).

Job request text (jobs/2026-11-19-g10-rl-dryrun1.md), lines to change:
  Command: add  --sampler g5_batch  after  --origin g5_delivery
  Time section, after "because r is the unknown:" add: "B5 (23 Nov, Colab T4, T2 fp16, 16 x 8 x 1,536, stop disabled) measured
  r = 44.3 s with sampler policy and 3.45 s with sampler g5_batch (results/b5_sampler_2026-11-23.md); this job uses g5_batch,
  and its rate probe times the batched path."
  Estimate line in the header: "Estimate 46-81 minutes" -> unchanged (the table's r range 1-9.4 s now covers g5_batch).

